dbr:Dracula%3A_Dead_and_Loving_It a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "Dracula: Dead and Loving It"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "Dracula: Dead and Loving It is a 1995 gothic comedy horror film directed by Mel Brooks and starring Leslie Nielsen. It is a spoof of Bram Stoker's novel Dracula and of some of the story's well-known adaptations. Brooks co-authored the screenplay with Steve Haberman and Rudy De Luca. He also appears as Dr. Van Helsing. The film's other stars include Steven Weber, Amy Yasbeck, Peter MacNicol, Harvey Korman, and Anne Bancroft. The film follows the classic Dracula (1931), starring Bela Lugosi, in its deviations from the novel. Its visual style and production values are reminiscent of the Hammer Horror films. It spoofs, among other films, The Fearless Vampire Killers (1967) and Bram Stoker's Dracula (1992). As being a critical and commercial failure, it is currently the latest film directed by Mel Brooks."@en ;
    dbo:country "France" ;
    dbo:director "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mel_Brooks" ;
