dbr:Menace_II_Society a dbo:Film ;
    rdfs:label "Menace II Society"@en ;
    dbo:abstract "Menace II Society (pronounced Menace to Society) is a 1993 American teen drama film directed by the Hughes Brothers in their directorial debut. The film is set in Watts and Crenshaw neighborhoods of Los Angeles, and follows the life of Kaydee \"Caine\" Lawson (Tyrin Turner) and his close friends. It gained notoriety for its scenes of violence, profanity, and drug-related content, and also received critical acclaim for the performances of Turner, Jada Pinkett, and Larenz Tate, the direction, and its realistic portrayal of urban violence and powerful underlying messages."@en ;
    dbo:country "United States" ;
    dbo:director "http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hughes_Brothers" ;
